Opt-in draw trace for chosen native shaders. EDEN_NX2_TRACE_DRAW_KEYS (set by the PS5 frontend
from /data/eden-nx2/trace-draws.txt) names native shader keys. The key of each lowered native
program is recorded by address in shader_environment.cpp; for a few frames, every draw whose
vertex or pixel program has a traced key logs one NX2_DRAW_TRACE line: the draw kind (direct,
indirect, issued by a macro), counts, firsts, base vertex and instance, topology, the host draw
parameters, the indirect arguments as guest memory holds them and whether the buffer cache marks
them GPU modified, the macro's parameters and where they were read from, the vertex attributes,
each bound vertex stream and the index buffer with their GPU/CPU modified state, and the first
guest words of a few vertices. Off, it costs one static load per draw.

